  "scope_checks": [
    {
      "topic": "Domain and quantifiers",
      "finding": "Every open subset of EuclideanSpace real (Fin 2) with finite positive Lebesgue area; the original bounded smooth nonempty planar domain is included. Equal area is pi times R squared with R positive.",
      "sources": [
        "PlanarBucklingChallenge.lean:138-147",
        "PlanarBucklingSolution.lean:219-226"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Sobolev space and boundary condition",
      "finding": "H02 is the closure of actual smooth compactly supported value, first-derivative and second-derivative graphs in a finite product of L2 spaces. Equivalent finite-product norms give the standard H02 closure; for smooth domains this imposes both clamped traces. No positivity restriction is built into IsTestFn or H02.",
      "sources": [
        "PlanarBucklingChallenge.lean:39-78",
        "RequestProject/Core1.lean:4140-4201",
        "RequestProject/Core4.lean:172-208"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Eigenvalue and nonvacuity",
      "finding": "Squared L2 norm of the sum of diagonal second derivatives divided by the sum of squared first-derivative L2 norms. Nonzero denominator is required; nonempty admissible functions on every nonempty open domain are constructed with a smooth bump. The quotient is nonnegative and the infimum is bounded below; this is not an empty-infimum proof.",
      "sources": [
        "PlanarBucklingChallenge.lean:82-102",
        "RequestProject/Core2.lean:2025-2033",
        "RequestProject/Core2.lean:2152-2210"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Concrete definition bridges",
      "finding": "The complete challenge/solution mathematical-definition blocks agree after removing comments and whitespace. H02_eq and bucklingEig_eq identify them with the concrete proof objects; the toL2 fallback never applies to the test functions or their derivatives, since their MemLp facts are proved.",
      "sources": [
        "PlanarBucklingSolution.lean:146-196",
        "RequestProject/Core1.lean:4161-4193"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "No hidden extra hypothesis",
      "finding": "The final theorem has only the natural geometric/area/radius hypotheses. The older intermediate Core4 theorem accepts PaperExternals, whose sole field is Faber-Krahn; UnconditionalFaberKrahn constructs that package from proved results and UnconditionalAreaRigidity supplies it. No sign, connectedness, topology or unproved theorem-package assumption is passed by the user.",
      "sources": [
        "RequestProject/Core1.lean:4702-4716",
        "UnconditionalFaberKrahn.lean:30-53",
        "UnconditionalAreaRigidity.lean:29-46",
        "PlanarBucklingSolution.lean:219-226"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Disk comparison and constants",
      "finding": "The conclusion is an actual bucklingEig comparison against the same-area metric disk, with exact open-disk equality. Bessel functions use their power series and positive zero infima; the disk eigenvalue is proved. The buckling denominator is gradient energy, distinct from clamped-plate vibration.",
      "sources": [
        "PlanarBucklingChallenge.lean:105-147",
        "RequestProject/Core4.lean:1013-1021",
        "RequestProject/Core4.lean:1128-1159"
      ]
    }
  ],
